@startuml
title Janus — signup and eventual account provisioning
actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Auth Lambda" as Auth
participant "Amazon Cognito" as Cognito
queue "SQS account queue" as Queue
participant "Provision Lambda" as Provision
database "Account DynamoDB" as DB
Client -> Gateway: POST /signup (usage-plan API key)
Gateway -> Auth: Invoke
Auth -> Cognito: AdminCreateUser
Cognito --> Auth: User sub
Auth -> Queue: Send account-created event
Auth --> Gateway: Identity accepted
Gateway --> Client: Response
Queue -> Provision: Deliver event (at least once)
Provision -> DB: Conditional PutItem\nattribute_not_exists(id)
DB --> Provision: Inserted or already exists
note over Auth, DB
Cognito create and SQS enqueue are not atomic.
Missing event / poison message recovery remains a gap.
end note
Client -> Gateway: GET /account (API key + ID token)
Gateway -> Cognito: Validate ID token via user-pool authorizer
Cognito --> Gateway: Verified claims
Gateway -> Provision: (no direct invocation)
note right of Gateway
The account HTTP Lambda uses the validated
sub as the DynamoDB record key.
end note
@enduml
